    "body": "## Independent exact-head review - PR444 participant read hardening, CI transport follow-up\n\n**Reviewed HEAD:** `bc3687ec582c8f23aab0725c772641afb79942bd`, single parent `f8d8a3f8e89625745bad682f0659971a0b2c8fb2`. Existing [Draft PR444](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/pull/444) remains OPEN/DRAFT/UNMERGED, clean/mergeable, stacked on PR443 head `c0e6ccb11d8302b1e6f7095a063d5c93f5313f98`. Compared to previous head: 1 ahead/0 behind and **only** `gameplay-server/test/private_api_local_test.mjs` changed (+199/-44); production `src/worker.js`, SQL migrations and workflows unchanged in this final commit.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS_NARROW_PARTICIPANT_READ_HARDENING` / no deployment or full credential lifecycle authorization.** Direct diff inspection confirms real HTTP requests are not retried; test harness sets `connection: close` rather than reusing long-idle pooled sockets across synchronous Wrangler D1 CLI operations. Temporary test-only wrapper is written into the isolated temporary directory and wraps the actual Worker/D1 binding to deterministically change generation immediately after the initial authorization SELECT, before subsequent authorized state/receipt queries. No production test-control endpoint is added. Separate status-active/generation-change and current-generation/status-revoked HTTP cases assert 401 and no gameplay/receipt/outbox writes; successful A/B, replay, restart, reveal/expire and revoke race scenarios remain.\n\n**Independently verified exact-head GitHub Actions and job logs:** [Private API 40161649615](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40161649615) SUCCESS, actual isolated workerd/D1 migration 0001-0005 PASS and new Worker HTTP generation-race + status-only revocation tests PASS, 22/22 offline harness tests PASS; [CAS SQL 40161649659](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40161649659) SUCCESS, 50/50 Python tests and separate legacy Wrangler CAS PASS; [AI Forensics 40161649612](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/40161649612) SUCCESS. End-of-test diagnostic reports 89 synchronous D1 operations, total 120,454 ms, max 1,681 ms, Worker still running (`exitCode=null`, `signalCode=null`) in the new successful run.\n\n**Do not overclaim historical root cause:** previous `UND_ERR_SOCKET` had no captured process state; stale pooled keep-alive reuse remains plausible, not proved. Success with request-level close is sufficient for current acceptance but not a backward proof about previous crash. Current local workerd integration is not hosted D1 acceptance.\n\n**Outstanding release blockers:** migration `0003` admin create replay can still decrypt and return original credentials after invalidation; no finalized rotation/revoke lifecycle or recovery closure in live schema; legacy generation=1 does not establish original issuance; invite-only human trust model, retention, key management/backup and hosted testing remain unapproved. Preserve user checkpoint+recovery gate and all Draft PRs; no main merge/production/Cloudflare/deploy permission. Local lost-SSD event reported by user: exact remote HEAD and PR verified, not evidence that uncommitted local-only files are backed up. Next separate task should tackle creation-recovery closure, not more polishing this transport test.",
